cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
title: "pollen"
abstract: >-
  Live audience questions for a talk or a class, with no accounts and nothing
  kept afterwards. Multiple choice, rating scales, rankings, word clouds and
  audience questions with support votes; any choice question can carry a right
  answer, which adds a scoreboard, and any question can be timed by the server.
  The room joins by typing a six-character code or scanning a QR code and
  answers on their phones, while the results build on the projected screen. Any
  question can carry a picture, rescaled in the browser to stay under 100 KB.
  Runs as a single Cloudflare Worker with one Durable Object per room, which is
  both the storage and the point every vote passes through; a room deletes
  itself twelve hours after it opens. No login, no cookie, no analytics and no
  third-party request of any kind. Multilingual (EN/DE/ES). It runs on
  Cloudflare or on any machine with Node from the same code, deployable to
  anyone's own account or server with nothing to configure and no database to
  connect.
